   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Text Animator\n\nlayer-animator style text animator: a range selector sweeps across the characters, words or lines and drives position, scale, rotation, skew, opacity, blur, tracking and fill colour of what it covers.\n\nCategory: typography. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- You want a layer-animator style animator: one selector window sliding across the text, with the properties of your choice applied to what it covers.\n- A flexible per-character, per-word or per-line reveal where position, scale, rotation, blur, tracking and colour can be mixed.\n\nAvoid when:\n- A plain staggered entrance is enough: use split-text-chars.\n- You need a wiggly (noise) selector or per-glyph character substitution: this port has the range selector only.\n\nVariables:\n- text (string): Text, default \"Animate every letter.\"\n- font_size (number, 24-260): Font size, default 84\n- color (color): Color, default \"#f4f4f5\"\n- font_weight (number, 100-900): Font weight, default 700\n- font (enum): Font, default \"geist\"\n- based_on (enum): Based on, default \"characters\"\n- position_x (number, -3-3): Position X, default 0\n- position_y (number, -3-3): Position Y, default 0.5\n- scale (number, 0-3): Scale, default 0.8\n- rotation (number, -360-360): Rotation, default 0\n- skew (number, -60-60): Skew, default 0\n- opacity (number, 0-1): Opacity, default 0\n- blur (number, 0-60): Blur, default 10\n- tracking (number, -1-3): Tracking, default 0\n- fill_color (color): Fill color, default \"#7dd3fc\"\n- use_fill (boolean): Use fill color, default true\n- shape (enum): Selector shape, default \"square\"\n- smoothness (number, 0-1): Smoothness, default 1\n- start (number, -100-200): Start, default 0\n- end (number, -100-200): End, default 100\n- offset_from (number, -200-200): Offset from, default 0\n- offset_to (number, -200-200): Offset to, default 100\n- random_order (boolean): Random order, default false\n- seed (number, 0-999): Seed, default 1\n- delay_frames (number, 0-300): Delay, default 8\n- sweep_frames (number, 4-300): Sweep, default 60\n\nSource: https://github.com/riaz37/remotion-ui. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
